    "If you kept only the `k` largest values seen so far, which of them would be the answer at the end?",
    "Keep a min-heap of at most `k` values. Push each number; whenever the heap holds more than `k`, pop its smallest. At the end the heap's minimum is the `k`-th largest. (In JavaScript, sorting a copy is fine if you have no heap.)",
    "Parallel example: to find the third-fastest runner as results arrive, keep a podium of three; a new time only gets on if it beats the slowest person on the podium."
